1
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,322
Every day your reps knock on doors.

2
00:00:05,322 --> 00:00:07,861
Some of those houses need you right now.

3
00:00:07,861 --> 00:00:11,987
Most don’t. Traverse tells you which is which before anyone leaves the truck.

4
00:00:14,187 --> 00:00:19,183
Traverse puts the facts that matter to your trade on every house in your area,

5
00:00:19,183 --> 00:00:21,515
and ranks the doors worth knocking first.

6
00:00:23,715 --> 00:00:26,644
Then it runs everything after the knock: the quote,

7
00:00:26,644 --> 00:00:29,573
the signature, the deposit, the job and the follow-up.

8
00:00:29,573 --> 00:00:34,130
One app, on the phone in the field and the computer in the office.

9
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:36,082
Here it is for three trades.

10
00:00:39,882 --> 00:00:43,010
For roofers, it starts with the storm.

11
00:00:43,910 --> 00:00:46,742
Open Storms and every storm day is there,

12
00:00:46,742 --> 00:00:50,637
with the hail size and the path drawn over your map.

13
00:00:53,137 --> 00:00:57,265
Tap a day and you get the houses it reached, biggest hail first.

14
00:00:59,465 --> 00:01:06,392
Every house shows the hail it took, storm by storm, the damaging wind nearby, the roof’s size and pitch,

15
00:01:06,392 --> 00:01:11,861
what it’s made of and how old it is, and whether it’s been re-roofed since.

16
00:01:11,861 --> 00:01:15,872
New owners are flagged too, with the month they moved in.

17
00:01:18,072 --> 00:01:20,361
The best doors rise to the top.

18
00:01:20,361 --> 00:01:23,959
A manager ticks a street and assigns it to a rep.

19
00:01:26,159 --> 00:01:29,247
It’s on their phone before they leave the lot.

20
00:01:31,447 --> 00:01:36,974
Live radar and storm alerts let you know the moment severe weather hits your towns.

21
00:01:38,374 --> 00:01:43,422
For lawn and landscape companies, the card shows the lawn before you pull up.

22
00:01:44,322 --> 00:01:49,466
Its size in square feet, the property line on the photo with the lawn shaded in,

23
00:01:49,466 --> 00:01:54,289
how much of it sits near the house, and the trees close to the house.

24
00:01:56,789 --> 00:01:59,596
It even knows the town’s watering days.

25
00:02:01,796 --> 00:02:05,764
Quote from the lawn’s own size, at your own prices.

26
00:02:07,964 --> 00:02:10,451
The homeowner signs on their phone.

27
00:02:12,651 --> 00:02:15,179
And you take the deposit right there.

28
00:02:17,379 --> 00:02:19,226
Mark the job done.

29
00:02:21,426 --> 00:02:26,514
After the job, the aftercare tips and your review link go out on their own.

30
00:02:29,614 --> 00:02:35,093
For solar teams, every roof shows its sun-facing area, the shade from tall trees,

31
00:02:35,093 --> 00:02:40,181
the system that fits it, and a year’s output for that exact spot.

32
00:02:42,381 --> 00:02:46,668
Houses that already have solar are moved down, so nobody wastes a knock.

33
00:02:48,868 --> 00:02:51,836
The proposal starts from the roof.

34
00:02:54,036 --> 00:02:56,803
And the homeowner signs it on the spot.

35
00:02:58,203 --> 00:02:59,971
Back at the office,

36
00:03:00,871 --> 00:03:03,598
every lead is in one pipeline.

37
00:03:06,098 --> 00:03:10,545
Connect your Facebook lead ads and new leads land in the pipeline.

38
00:03:12,745 --> 00:03:15,713
Draw territories and see who knocked what.

39
00:03:17,913 --> 00:03:22,040
And get a picture of the day by email, every night.

40
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:28,267
Traverse. The all-in-one sales platform for the field and office.

41
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:32,128
See it with your own area at traverseplatforms.com.
